<p>Loyalty points reward regulars: they earn points on what they buy and spend them at the till like money. There are no cards; points
  belong to the customer's name in HardPoint, found by name or phone number at the till.</p>

<h2>Switching it on</h2>
<p>Owners and managers go to <strong>Settings › Loyalty points</strong>, tick <strong>Customers earn and spend points</strong>, and choose:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Points per KES 100</strong>: 1 means a customer spending KES 2,500 earns 25 points.</li>
  <li><strong>A point is worth</strong>: with KES 1, 25 points take KES 25 off a later purchase.</li>
  <li><strong>Spend from</strong>: the fewest points a customer can spend at once.</li>
</ul>
<p>The page shows what the scheme gives back as a percentage, and what all unspent points are worth.</p>

<h2>At the till</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Choose the customer before taking payment. Their points show under their name.</li>
  <li>Points are earned when the sale is paid for, on everything except the part paid with points.</li>
  <li>To spend points, choose <strong>Points</strong> as the payment method and enter how much to take off (or leave the amount as it is to
    use as many as cover the bill). Pay the rest as usual.</li>
  <li>The receipt shows the points earned and the new balance.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Voids, returns and corrections</h2>
<p>Voiding a sale takes its earned points back and returns any points spent on it. A return takes back its share of the points earned.
  Owners and managers can add or take off points on the customer's page, with a reason; every change is listed there.</p>

<h2>Points that expire</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Points expire</strong>, choose <strong>Never</strong> or a number of months. Points earned in a month run out at the end of
  the month that many months later: with 12 months, points earned any day in October 2025 run out on 31 October 2026. Customers spend
  their oldest points first, so points they've used come off the points that would run out soonest.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Points customers already have when you turn expiry on, or shorten it, count from that day. No one loses points on the day you
    change the rule.</li>
  <li>Points run out overnight at the start of the month. The customer's page shows when their next points run out and lists every
    expiry. The settings page shows how many points run out at the end of this month.</li>
  <li>Points only expire while the scheme is switched on.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Texts about points</h2>
<p>With SMS on for the shop (<strong>Settings › SMS</strong>), tick <strong>Text customers about their points</strong>. Customers with a
  phone number then get:</p>
<ul>
  <li>a text after each sale with the points earned, their balance and when the next points run out;</li>
  <li>one warning in the last 14 days of a month when some of their points run out at its end.</li>
</ul>
<p>Anyone can text a customer their balance with <strong>Text points balance</strong> on the customer's page. Every text is listed
  under <strong>Settings › SMS › Texts sent</strong>.</p>
